  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Hand Count\n\nA number that counts up in stop-motion poses, rewritten by hand at every pose.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A stat, price, or count belongs in a hand-made scene: the number should arrive by being written, not by rolling.\n- A paper pricing reveal or year-in-review needs its figure in the same voice as the rest of the shot.\n- A unit or currency should be written in the same hand as the digits: prefix and suffix jitter along with them.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The scene is a slick product UI or a dashboard metric: use rolling-number or number-wheel.\n- You need per-digit odometer choreography: that is number-wheel's job.\n- You need locale grouping separators (1,000) or full currency formatting; prefix and decimals are the whole surface here.\n\nVariables:\n- to (number, 0-10000): Count to, default 1284\n- from (number, 0-1000): Count from, default 0\n- delay (number, 0-120): Delay, default 0\n- duration_steps (number, 2-24): Poses counting, default 18\n- decimals (number, 0-2): Decimals, default 0\n- prefix (string): Prefix, default \"\"\n- suffix (string): Suffix, default \"\"\n- font_size (number, 32-300): Font size, default 96\n- color (color): Color, default \"#26242c\"\n- weight (enum): Font weight, default \"700\"\n- ease (enum): Ease, default \"in-out\"\n- align (enum): Align, default \"center\"\n- seed (string): Seed, default \"count\"\n- step (number, 1-6): Frames per pose, default 3\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Hand Count\n\n  A number that counts up in stop-motion poses, rewritten by hand at every pose.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/hand-count/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"hand-count\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"to\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Count to\", \"description\": \"Final number.\", \"default\": 1284, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 10000, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"from\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Count from\", \"description\": \"Starting number.\", \"default\": 0, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1000, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"delay\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Delay\", \"description\": \"Frames before counting starts (30 fps).\", \"default\": 0, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 120, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"duration_steps\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Poses counting\", \"description\": \"Stop-motion poses the count takes.\", \"default\": 18, \"min\": 2, \"max\": 24, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"decimals\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Decimals\", \"description\": \"Digits after the decimal point.\", \"default\": 0, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 2, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"prefix\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Prefix\", \"description\": \"Written before the number, for example Rp.\", \"default\": \"\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suffix\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Suffix\", \"description\": \"Written after the number, for example %.\", \"default\": \"\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. Wider numbers shrink to fit.\", \"default\": 96, \"min\": 32, \"max\": 300, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Ink color.\", \"default\": \"#26242c\"},\n    {\"id\": \"weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the handwriting.\", \"default\": \"700\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"ease\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Ease\", \"description\": \"Pacing of the count.\", \"default\": \"in-out\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"in-out\", \"label\": \"In-out\"}, {\"value\": \"out\", \"label\": \"Out\"}, {\"value\": \"linear\", \"label\": \"Linear\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"align\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Align\", \"description\": \"Where the number sits.\", \"default\": \"center\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"center\", \"label\": \"Center\"}, {\"value\": \"left\", \"label\": \"Left\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"seed\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Seed\", \"description\": \"Any text; changes the per-pose wobble.\", \"default\": \"count\"},\n    {\"id\": \"step\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Frames per pose\", \"description\": \"Stop-motion clock, in frames at 30 fps.\", \"default\": 3, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 6, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Hand Count</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Caveat:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .hc-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; }\n        .hc-line { display: inline-block; font-family: Caveat, cursive; line-height: 1.15; white-space: pre; }\n        .hc-char { display: inline-block; white-space: pre; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"hand-count\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"hc-clip\" class=\"hc-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <span id=\"hc-line\" class=\"hc-line\"></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function col(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            function fit(el, maxPx, size, ratio) {\n              // Shrink el's font size until its scrollWidth fits ratio of the frame width.\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var max = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * (ratio || 0.9));\n              if (el.scrollWidth > max) { size = Math.max(10, size * (max / el.scrollWidth)); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function ease(name, a, b, c, d) { return CustomEase.create(name, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\"); }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            function ip(t, a, b, from, to, e) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : (t - a) / (b - a);\n              p = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p));\n              if (e) p = e(p);\n              return from + (to - from) * p;\n            }\n            function hash01(seed) {\n              var h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < seed.length; i++) { h ^= seed.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            function hashRange(seed, lo, hi) { return lo + hash01(seed) * (hi - lo); }\n            // Snap a frame number down to a stop-motion pose.\n            function qf(frame, step) { return Math.floor(frame / step + 1e-6) * step; }\n            function kf(t, keys, vals, e) {\n              if (t <= keys[0]) return vals[0];\n              for (var i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) if (t <= keys[i + 1]) return ip(t, keys[i], keys[i + 1], vals[i], vals[i + 1], e);\n              return vals[vals.length - 1];\n            }\n            // Per-frame drawing: a pure function of the timeline time, run from a tween's onUpdate.\n            function tick(draw) {\n              tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(tl.time()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var cubOut = ease(\"cub-out\", 0.215, 0.61, 0.355, 1);\n            var cubIn = ease(\"cub-in\", 0.55, 0.055, 0.675, 0.19);\n            var cubInOut = ease(\"cub-io\", 0.645, 0.045, 0.355, 1);\n\n            var stage = document.getElementById(\"hc-clip\");\n            var line = document.getElementById(\"hc-line\");\n            var to = num(vars.to, 1284, 0, 1000000), from = num(vars.from, 0, 0, 1000000);\n            var delay = num(vars.delay, 0, 0, 120), poses = num(vars.duration_steps, 18, 2, 24);\n            var decimals = num(vars.decimals, 0, 0, 2), step = num(vars.step, 3, 1, 6);\n            var prefix = typeof vars.prefix === \"string\" ? vars.prefix : \"\", suffix = typeof vars.suffix === \"string\" ? vars.suffix : \"\";\n            var seed = str(vars.seed, \"count\");\n            var easeName = pick(vars.ease, [\"in-out\", \"out\", \"linear\"], \"in-out\");\n            var align = pick(vars.align, [\"center\", \"left\"], \"center\");\n            var eases = {\n              \"in-out\": function (p) { return p < 0.5 ? 4 * p * p * p : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * p + 2, 3) / 2; },\n              out: function (p) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - p, 3); },\n              linear: function (p) { return p; }\n            };\n            stage.style.justifyContent = align === \"center\" ? \"center\" : \"flex-start\";\n            if (align === \"left\") stage.style.paddingLeft = \"4%\";\n            line.style.color = col(vars.color, \"#26242c\");\n            line.style.fontWeight = pick(vars.weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"700\");\n            function textFor(v) { return prefix + v.toFixed(decimals) + suffix; }\n            line.textContent = textFor(Math.max(from, to));\n            fit(line, 0, num(vars.font_size, 96, 32, 300), 0.9);\n            var settled = Math.ceil((delay + poses * step) / step) * step;\n            tick(function (t) {\n              var frame = Math.floor(t * 30 + 1e-6);\n              var f = qf(frame, step);\n              var end = delay + poses * step;\n              var progress = f <= delay ? 0 : f >= end ? 1 : eases[easeName]((f - delay) / (end - delay));\n              var value = from + (to - from) * progress;\n              var pose = Math.min(Math.floor(Math.max(0, frame) / step + 1e-6), Math.floor(settled / step + 1e-6));\n              var chars = Array.from(textFor(value));\n              line.textContent = \"\";\n              chars.forEach(function (ch, i) {\n                var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n                s.className = \"hc-char\"; s.textContent = ch;\n                var rot = hashRange(seed + \":\" + pose + \":\" + i + \":r\", -3.2, 3.2), dy = hashRange(seed + \":\" + pose + \":\" + i + \":y\", -1.8, 1.8);\n                s.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + dy + \"px) rotate(\" + rot + \"deg)\";\n                line.appendChild(s);\n              });\n            });\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"hand-count\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
